questions.question:
For the piecewise function \[
f(x)=\begin{cases} x+1,&x<0,\\ x^2,&x\ge0,\end{cases}
\] find \(f(-2)+f(2)\).

questions.explanation:
The curves intersect when \(x^2=2x\), so \(x=0\) or \(x=2\). On \(0\le x\le2\), \(2x\ge x^2\). The area is \[
\int_0^2 (2x-x^2)\,dx=\left[x^2-\frac{x^3}{3}\right]_0^2=4-\frac{8}{3}=\frac{4}{3}
\].
